  "summary": "Recent releases curate hundreds to thousands of single-cell and spatial datasets, shifting emphasis toward integrated cross-platform infrastructure.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is curated infrastructure for single-cell and spatial transcriptomics: databases, atlases and workflows that consolidate heterogeneous datasets rather than introduce new inference methods. Cell3D curates 898 single-cell and spatial datasets with interactive 2D/3D visualization, SpatialRegNet quantifies spot-level activity of 6733 TF regulons across 1322 human and mouse slices, and STRAND harmonizes 35 subcellular-resolution datasets. CellMarker 3.0 extends marker resources with predicted markers from six algorithms, while CellMethMarker provides 347,514 de novo cell- and tissue-type DNA methylation markers. Spatialsnake standardizes analysis across Visium, Visium HD, Stereo-seq, Xenium and MERFISH. Analytical studies, including CATFISHR for malignant cell identification and a 244-sample CTCL atlas, apply such data to distinct biological questions. What is new is breadth of cross-platform integration rather than a single algorithmic advance.",
